Republican [[Alan Wilson (politician)|Alan Wilson]], Democrat Matthew Richardson, and Green Party candidate Leslie Wilson were the nominees for [[Attorney General of South Carolina|attorney general]].  Wilson is the son of controversial South Carolina Congressman [[Joe Wilson (U.S. politician)|Joe Wilson]].  The race was marked by high fundraising totals for both Wilson and Richardson, second only to the governor's race in total money raised and spent in the general election.  Wilson eventually won.

In the Republican primary, Wilson faced two other challengers: [[Columbia, South Carolina|Columbia]] attorneys Leighton Lord and Robert Bolchoz.  Wilson eventually defeated Leighton Lord in a run-off.

