===Superintendent of Education===
Candidates for Superintendent of Education in South Carolina included Republican [[Mick Zais]], Democrat [[Frank Holleman]], and third-party candidates Doretha Bull, Tony Fayyazi, and Tim Moultrie.  Zais did little campaigning in the general, despite the relatively high fundraising totals posted by Holleman, a former [[United States Deputy Secretary of Education]] and South Carolina State Democratic Party Chairman.  The general election race became the third most expensive statewide race in South Carolina in 2010, and one of the higher profile, in part because the perception that the outcome could be as close as it had been in [[South Carolina state elections, 2006|2006]].  However, Zais eventually won.

Zais, a retired brigadier general and president of [[Newberry College]], defeated Elizabeth Moffly in the GOP primary run-off.  Moffly, a 2006 candidate for the Republican nomination, did surprisingly well considering her low fundraising and poor result in the [[2006 South Carolina state elections|2006 contest]].  Other candidates included: Kelly Payne, an [[Irmo, South Carolina|Irmo]] teacher; Gary Burgess, a former [[Laurens County, South Carolina|Laurens County]] school administrator who was arrested in 2009 for soliciting an immoral act;<ref name="Former Anderson School District 4 superintendent arrested">{{cite web|url=http://www.independentmail.com/news/2009/apr/30/former-district-4-superintendent-arrested/|title=Former Anderson School District 4 superintendent arresteds |work=Anderson Independent-Mail|date=April 3, 2009|access-date=December 21, 2012}}</ref> Brent Nelsen, a political science professor at [[Furman University]]; and Glenn Price, a [[Kershaw, South Carolina|Kershaw]] band teacher.  Moffly went on to be elected to the [[Charleston County, South Carolina|Charleston County]] School District Board of Trustees in November.<ref name="CCSD Board of Trustees Members">{{cite web|url=http://www.ccsdschools.com/Board_of_Trustees/Members/|title=CCSD Board of Trustees Members|work=CCSD|access-date=December 21, 2012}}</ref>

